# Check out every text file with LF, on every platform. Without this the
# Windows runner's `core.autocrlf=true` turned `.rs` files CRLF at checkout, and
# any test that scans a source file for a `\n`-joined literal matched nothing
# there and nowhere else (PRD #1105's selection-capture guard, fixed in
# 7b891592). No file in the index is stored CRLF and none needs a CRLF checkout
# (no .bat/.cmd/.ps1), so this renormalizes nothing. `text=auto` leaves files
# git detects as binary untouched. docs/develop/windows-cross-check.md has the
# recurring Windows-only failure shapes this does and does not cover.
* text=auto eol=lf

.github/workflows/*.lock.yml linguist-generated=true
